(7688064, 1259218, 30049, '<td valign="top">Thanks.  While I appreciate the comment, honestly, I wouldn''t change a thing with this photo.  I really liked the color, tone, and feel of it.  It was actually intentional.  :-)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BJokerud:</b></div><hr/><i> 1...c5 from me. The "black" pieces suits this technique better. all eht hightligs in the white pieces makes the photo a bit messy for my taste. It could potentially look cleaner if you had desaturated the reds and yellows a bit, removing the yellow color cast from the white pieces. Then the white hightligs would blend in better on the whiter white pieces. Desaturating the green sider could also make the glass look "glassier". </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks.  While I appreciate the comment, honestly, I wouldn''t change a thing with this photo.  I really liked the color, tone, and feel of it.  It was actually intentional.  :-) Originally posted by BJokerud: 1...c5 from me. The "black" pieces suits this technique better. all eht hightligs in the white pieces makes the photo a bit messy for my taste. It could potentially look cleaner if you had desaturated the reds and yellows a bit, removing the yellow color cast from the white pieces. Then the white hightligs would blend in better on the whiter white pieces. Desaturating the green sider could also make the glass look "glassier". ', '2021-02-26 07:57:54.000000', NULL, 0),
